From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu, memory: mediatek: add MT6897

The MT6897 has two multimedia IOMMUs of the second generation, one for the
display side and one for the MDP side. They walk one page table, as the two
of the MT8195 do. Each larb hangs on one of them through its SMI common.

Add the compatibles of the IOMMUs, the SMI common and the SMI larb, and the
port numbers of the video decoder, which is the first user: larb4 (core) is
on the MDP IOMMU and larb5 (front end) on the display IOMMU. The numbers
are those of the MediaTek header in the OnePlus MT6897 kernel
(include/dt-bindings/memory/mt6897-larb-port.h), without its page table and
domain fields.
